  "title": "Hardy-Littlewood Conjecture F (Primes in Quadratic Polynomials)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For a polynomial $f(x) = ax^2 + bx + c$ with $a > 0$, $\\gcd(a,b,c) = 1$, and discriminant $\\Delta = b^2 - 4ac$ not a perfect square, the polynomial takes infinitely many prime values. Furthermore, the number $P(n)$ of primes of the form $f(x) \\leq n$ satisfies an asymptotic formula $P(n) \\sim A \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{n}}{\\log n}$ where $A$ depends on $a, b, c$ but not on $n$.",
